/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (A Virtual Synchronous Generator \(VSG\) is a software-based control technique that uses mathematical algorithms to emulate the dynamic behaviour of a conventional synchronous generator, including inertia, damping, and power-angle characteristics. It enables inverters to respond to grid frequency variations like synchronous generators and implement frequency-power droop control, allowing multiple inverters to share electrical loads automatically while improving grid stability.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
